// ---- people: 16x24 billboard frames, 4-bit, feet on the frame's bottom row. A person kind k
// (ART_PK_*) has a sheet of 9 frame columns (ART_FR_* / ART_PPL_FRAME_*) by 4 direction rows
// (ART_DIR_* / ART_PPL_DIR_*): frame f, direction d is the 16x24 cell at
//   u = ART_PERSON_U[k] + f * 16, v = ART_PERSON_V[k] + d * 24 in slot ART_PERSON_SLOT[k],
// drawn with 4-bit palette ART_PERSON_PAL[k]. Directions are screen-relative: 0 toward the viewer
// facing screen-right, 1 toward the viewer facing screen-left, 2 away facing screen-left, 3 away
// facing screen-right (with the camera looking from +x+z: walking +z -> 0, +x -> 1, -z -> 2,
// -x -> 3). "use" has the arms forward (counter, stove); "swim" is head and shoulders, the frame's
// bottom rows are the water line.
